# REST API Conventions

## HTTP Status Codes
| Situation | Code |
|---|---|
| Resource created | `201 Created` (with `Location` header) |
| Successful with no body | `204 No Content` |
| Resource not found | `404 Not Found` |
| Duplicate / conflict | `409 Conflict` |
| Validation error | `422 Unprocessable Entity` |
| Generic success | `200 OK` |

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD
[HttpPost]
public ActionResult<EventResponse> CriarEvento([FromBody] EventRequest request)
{
    var response = _eventService.CriarEvento(request);
    return CreatedAtAction(nameof(BuscarPorId), new { id = response.Id }, response);
}

[HttpDelete("{id}")]
public IActionResult DeletarEvento(long id)
{
    _eventService.DeletarEvento(id);
    return NoContent();
}
```

## Validation
Use DataAnnotations on record DTOs. `[ApiController]` validates ModelState automatically —
configure `InvalidModelStateResponseFactory` to return `422 Unprocessable Entity` with an
`ErrorResponse` body instead of the default 400.

```csharp
public record EventRequest(
    [property: Required] string Titulo,
    string Descricao,
    [property: Required] DateTime DataHora,
    string Local,
    [property: Required][property: Range(1, int.MaxValue)] int LimiteVagas);
```

## Centralized Error Handling
Use a single exception-handling middleware — never catch domain exceptions in controllers.

- `ResourceNotFoundException` → 404
- `ConflictException` → 409
- `ArgumentException` → 422
- Any other `Exception` → 500 with generic message

## Response Format
All responses must be JSON (camelCase, Portuguese domain attributes). Error body is
`{ "mensagem": "..." }`. Never return plain strings from controllers.
